<%#
  One more item in Redmine's *Copy project* checkbox list: this project's own
  workflow (finding F01 of 2026-08-28 second run, and Jan's question the day
  after -- the first answer copied the workflow unconditionally and said so only
  in the README).

  Rendered through core's own `view_projects_copy_only_items` hook, which sits
  inside that fieldset on 5.1, 6.1 and 7.0 alike -- so this needs no Deface
  override and INV-9's count stays at fifteen. The seam is core's API rather
  than a selector, but it can still go away, so
  spec/controllers/projects_copy_form_spec.rb asserts the checkbox reaches the
  rendered page on every supported version, exactly as INV-9's spec does for the
  overrides.

  Core's markup verbatim: the same `<label class="block">`, the same `only[]`
  name (which core's own toggle-all link selects on), the same `:id => nil`, and
  the same "(count)" after the label. Nothing here is styled by the plugin.

  Checked by default, like every one of core's items. The parameter can
  therefore only ever *narrow* what is copied, never widen it, which is what
  keeps a checkbox off INV-7's list of ways a request can reach further than the
  screen offered.

  Locals: project -- the *source* project (core passes it as `project`), plus
  whatever else call_hook puts in the context.
%>
<% key = RedmineProjectWorkflows::Services::ProjectWorkflowCopier::COPY_ONLY_KEY %>
<% scope_count = ProjectWorkflowScope.where(project_id: project.id).count %>
<label class="block"><%= check_box_tag 'only[]', key, true, id: nil %> <%= l(:label_project_workflow_copy_item) %> (<%= scope_count %>)</label>
